## When to use `variables=[...]` on `delegate_to_...`

Use the optional **`variables`** argument when the **sub-agent must receive concrete data** you already have under variable names—so it can use those objects (lists, dicts, IDs, etc.), not only your natural-language **`task`** string.

**Prefer including `variables` when:**
- **Handoff:** Agent A returned structured data and agent B must act on **that same payload** — e.g. `variables=["customer_list"]`.
- **Several facts:** The downstream agent needs **multiple** named pieces of context.
- **A2A / metadata:** When the tool docs say variables are passed in metadata.

**Workflow:** After values exist in **Variables**, delegate in a **later** execution with **`variables=["..."]`**. If the job is fully described in **`task`** alone, omit **`variables`**.

